    "## 9. Analysis\n\n### Workflow\n\n```\nChristian's geocoded CSV (industrial_businesses_core_geocoded.csv)\n         \u2502\n         \u25bc\n[joseph_indicators_v10.ipynb]\n  \u251c\u2500\u2500 Clip to SD planning districts (Community_Plan_SD.geojson)\n  \u251c\u2500\u2500 Assign subareas via spatial join (four study areas)\n  \u251c\u2500\u2500 Indicator 1:  dist_nearest_poe_mi     (geometry.distance \u2192 POE union)\n  \u251c\u2500\u2500 Indicator 1b: dist_to_freight_road_mi  (gpd.sjoin_nearest \u2192 roads)\n  \u2514\u2500\u2500 Indicator 2:  buffer_quarter/half/one_mi (binary inside/outside)\n         \u2502\n         \u25bc\n[joseph_indicators_output.geojson]  \u2190\u2500\u2500 loaded below\n         \u2502\n         \u25bc\n[joseph_visualizations_v8.ipynb]\n  \u251c\u2500\u2500 Map 1: Overview dot map (four subareas)\n  \u251c\u2500\u2500 Map 2: POE distance graduated color\n  \u251c\u2500\u2500 Map 3: Otay Mesa zoom \u2014 buffer rings\n  \u251c\u2500\u2500 Map 4: KDE heatmap 2\u00d72 grid\n  \u251c\u2500\u2500 Charts: Buffer overlap bar + POE distance box plot\n  \u2514\u2500\u2500 Stats:  Pairwise Mann-Whitney U + Chi-square + Effect sizes\n```\n\n### Step-by-Step Description\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 CRS selection**  \nAll spatial operations use EPSG:3310 (California Albers, meters), matching Christian's pipeline. Distances computed in meters, converted to miles for reporting.\n\n**Step 2 \u2014 Subarea assignment**  \nBusinesses assigned to study areas via `gpd.sjoin` on official City of San Diego Community Planning District boundaries. This matches Christian's `planning_area` approach and replaces the researcher-defined bounding box used in earlier versions.\n\n| Study Area | Planning Districts Used |\n|---|---|\n| Otay Mesa | OTAY MESA + OTAY MESA-NESTOR |\n| Kearny Mesa | KEARNY MESA |\n| Miramar | MIRAMAR RANCH NORTH + SCRIPPS MIRAMAR RANCH |\n| Sorrento Valley | MIRA MESA *(no official Sorrento Valley district)* |\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 Indicator 1: POE Distance**  \nEuclidean distance from each business point to the nearest SANDAG POE feature. Separate distances to San Ysidro and Otay Mesa POEs retained. Summarized by subarea with medians and means.\n\n**Step 4 \u2014 Indicator 1b: Freight Road Distance**  \n`gpd.sjoin_nearest()` against the SANDAG major roads layer assigns each business its distance to the nearest road segment. Distance category bins match Christian's: 0\u20130.25, 0.25\u20130.5, 0.5\u20131, 1\u20132, 2+ miles.\n\n**Step 5 \u2014 Indicator 2: Buffer Flags**  \nThe dissolved road network is buffered at 402m (0.25 mi), 805m (0.50 mi), and 1,609m (1.00 mi). Each business receives a binary inside/outside flag per buffer distance.\n\n**Step 6 \u2014 Statistical Testing**  \nPairwise comparisons \u2014 Otay Mesa vs each of the three comparison areas:\n- **Mann-Whitney U** on `dist_nearest_poe_mi` \u2014 non-parametric, appropriate for skewed distance distributions\n- **Chi-square + Cram\u00e9r's V** on each buffer flag \u2014 proportion test for binary outcomes\n- **95% bootstrap CIs** on all effect sizes (2,000 iterations)\n\n**Evolution from Proposal**  \nThe proposal anticipated industrial zone polygons and ESRI GeoEnrichment. Both replaced: polygons by geocoded records (leftover-land critique), GeoEnrichment by Census ACS API. Statistical significance testing was added based on the need to formally distinguish the Otay Mesa pattern from sampling variation.\n"
